{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>YHWH, how</b> — In the sacred language it falls upon something weighty and upon something contemptible, like מה רבו מעשיך, מה אנוש כי תזכרנו, and in this place, for astonishment. And Israel split into three parts: some of them are foes like the tribe of Benjamin, and some of them are those who rise up, and they are our kinsmen and Amasa and relatives. And others say: for he has fallen and will not rise again."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:07.798906060Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}